From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Mar 2026 03:54:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Prevent server from writing to config files

An existing server.properties, bukkit.yml, commands.yml, spigot.yml,
purpur.yml, or Paper configuration file (paper-global.yml,
paper-world-defaults.yml, per-world paper-world.yml) is never rewritten:
no comment or ordering churn and no default back-fill. A file that does
not exist yet is still generated with defaults, so a fresh instance
starts without copying configuration from another server.

Runtime changes that vanilla persisted to server.properties
(/whitelist on|off, /setidletimeout) now apply in memory only;
/whitelist tells the sender so. The legacy paper.yml conversion is
skipped for the same reason.

One INFO line at startup states the rule; skipped writes are silent.

